movsx from bp or sp: sign-extend

_lift_movsx listed the 16-bit source registers without bp and sp
(_lift_movzx has them), so `movsx ebp, bp` was lifted as a zero
extension: a negative 16-bit value became 0x0000FFFF. Found in Mad Dash
Recomp (Bink IDCT); carried here as 0048.

--- a/tools/recomp/lifter.py	2026-11-21 00:37:41.366388135 +0000
+++ b/tools/recomp/lifter.py	2026-11-21 00:37:41.367861928 +0000
@@ -1866,7 +1866,7 @@
             r = ops[1].reg
             if r in ("al", "bl", "cl", "dl", "ah", "bh", "ch", "dh"):
                 src = f"SX8({src})"
-            elif r in ("ax", "bx", "cx", "dx", "si", "di"):
+            elif r in ("ax", "bx", "cx", "dx", "si", "di", "bp", "sp"):
                 src = f"SX16({src})"
         return [_fmt_operand_write(ops[0], src)]
 
